{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function useHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequence.ts#L69","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useHotkeySequence.ts:69"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React hook for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This hook allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d'\nthat trigger when the full sequence is pressed within a timeout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+R"},{"type":"text","value":" then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Shift+T"},{"type":"text","value":"). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"sequence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sequence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeySequence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Array of hotkey strings that form the sequence"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"callback","children":[{"type":"text","value":"callback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HotkeyCallback"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function to call when the sequence is completed"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UseHotkeySequenceOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options for the sequence behavior. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enabled: false"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the registration (visible in devtools)\nand only suppresses firing; the hook updates the existing handle instead of unregistering."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function VimEditor() {\n  // 'g g' to go to top\n  useHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n    scrollToTop()\n  })\n\n  // 'd d' to delete line\n  useHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n    deleteLine()\n  })\n\n  // 'd i w' to delete inner word\n  useHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n    deleteInnerWord()\n  }, { timeout: 500 })\n\n  // Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\n  useHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n    nextAction()\n  })\n\n  return <div>...</div>\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"sequence","text":"sequence","level":3},{"id":"callback","text":"callback","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequence.ts:69](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequence.ts#L69)\n\nReact hook for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style).\n\nThis hook allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d'\nthat trigger when the full sequence is pressed within a timeout.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`HotkeySequence`\n\nArray of hotkey strings that form the sequence\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nFunction to call when the sequence is completed\n\n### options?\n\n[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nOptions for the sequence behavior. `enabled: false` keeps the registration (visible in devtools)\n  and only suppresses firing; the hook updates the existing handle instead of unregistering.\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction VimEditor() {\n  // 'g g' to go to top\n  useHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n    scrollToTop()\n  })\n\n  // 'd d' to delete line\n  useHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n    deleteLine()\n  })\n\n  // 'd i w' to delete inner word\n  useHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n    deleteInnerWord()\n  }, { timeout: 500 })\n\n  // Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\n  useHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n    nextAction()\n  })\n\n  return <div>...</div>\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useHotkeySequence\ntitle: useHotkeySequence\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction useHotkeySequence(\n   sequence, \n   callback, \n   options?): void;\n```\n\nDefined in: [useHotkeySequence.ts:69](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/react-hotkeys/src/useHotkeySequence.ts#L69)\n\nReact hook for registering a keyboard shortcut sequence (Vim-style).\n\nThis hook allows you to register multi-key sequences like 'g g' or 'd d'\nthat trigger when the full sequence is pressed within a timeout.\n\nEach step may include modifiers. You can chain the same modifier across\nsteps (e.g. `Shift+R` then `Shift+T`). Modifier-only keydown events (Shift,\nControl, Alt, or Meta pressed alone) are ignored while matching—they do not\nadvance the sequence or reset progress.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### sequence\n\n`HotkeySequence`\n\nArray of hotkey strings that form the sequence\n\n### callback\n\n`HotkeyCallback`\n\nFunction to call when the sequence is completed\n\n### options?\n\n[`UseHotkeySequenceOptions`](../interfaces/UseHotkeySequenceOptions.md) = `{}`\n\nOptions for the sequence behavior. `enabled: false` keeps the registration (visible in devtools)\n  and only suppresses firing; the hook updates the existing handle instead of unregistering.\n\n## Returns\n\n`void`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nfunction VimEditor() {\n  // 'g g' to go to top\n  useHotkeySequence(['G', 'G'], () => {\n    scrollToTop()\n  })\n\n  // 'd d' to delete line\n  useHotkeySequence(['D', 'D'], () => {\n    deleteLine()\n  })\n\n  // 'd i w' to delete inner word\n  useHotkeySequence(['D', 'I', 'W'], () => {\n    deleteInnerWord()\n  }, { timeout: 500 })\n\n  // Same modifier on consecutive steps (bare Shift between chords is ignored)\n  useHotkeySequence(['Shift+R', 'Shift+T'], () => {\n    nextAction()\n  })\n\n  return <div>...</div>\n}\n```\n"}
